    "citations": null,
    "text": "{\"related_campaigns\": [], \"kill_chain_stage\": \"initial access \u2192 execution \u2192 command and control\", \"prior_alert_context\": \"This alert represents an early-stage exploit attempt against a web API. If successful, the attacker would have achieved remote code execution and would likely progress to tool staging (via wget malware.sh) for persistence, lateral movement, or data exfiltration. Similar patterns often precede multi-stage attacks where initial reconnaissance (cat /etc/passwd) is paired with immediate payload delivery to establish a foothold. Expect to see follow-up alerts if the WAF had not blocked this: suspicious process execution, network outbound connections to malware.sh host, or lateral movement attempts.\", \"threat_severity_hint\": \"high\"}",
